WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.960
Three families in northern Pakistan had members who had never experienced pain.

2
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:16.780
The cause was two broken copies of one sodium channel gene, SCN9A.

3
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.300
That gene makes the channel Nav1.7.

4
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.700
In cultured cells, the mutant channels passed no current above background.

5
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.800
Lose this channel, lose pain.

6
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:39.863
Nociceptor spikes draw on three sodium channels: Nav1.7, Nav1.8, and Nav1.9.

7
00:00:40.863 --> 00:00:47.683
A selective blocker of Nav1.7 did not significantly beat placebo in one trial of

8
00:00:47.683 --> 00:00:49.283
painful diabetic neuropathy.

9
00:00:50.303 --> 00:00:56.803
The drug approved in the United States in January 2025 blocks Nav1.8 instead.

10
00:00:57.783 --> 00:01:00.383
Now, how is a blocker described?

11
00:01:01.363 --> 00:01:05.823
Take human Nav1.8, expressed in a cell line.

12
00:01:06.523 --> 00:01:10.623
A fitted curve links the drug concentration to the current that remains.

13
00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:15.203
Half the current remains at one concentration, called Kd.

14
00:01:16.043 --> 00:01:21.183
In this fit, Kd is 0.38 nanomolar, at 37 °C.

15
00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:28.227
Put in numbers. The fraction left is Kd over Kd plus the concentration.

16
00:01:29.107 --> 00:01:33.807
At 10 nanomolar, that leaves 3.66% of the current.

17
00:01:34.547 --> 00:01:40.327
To reach 99% block, the concentration must be 37.62 nanomolar.

18
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.890
Now ask the neuron.

19
00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:49.310
In dissociated sensory neurons from adult human organ donors, recorded at 37 °C,

20
00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:55.310
the blocker generally reduced repetitive firing, but did not eliminate it.

21
00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.630
At 10 nanomolar, it lowered the spike peak and the shoulder.

22
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:03.630
It largely spared threshold and the initial upstroke.

23
00:02:04.433 --> 00:02:06.833
Why does the neuron still fire?

24
00:02:07.673 --> 00:02:12.113
The authors' voltage-clamp analysis suggested two possible reasons.

25
00:02:12.893 --> 00:02:20.313
Many neurons carry such large Nav1.8 currents that even 99% block leaves

26
00:02:20.313 --> 00:02:22.033
nanoampere-level current.

27
00:02:22.713 --> 00:02:27.753
And Nav1.7 current dominates the initial spikes in these recordings.

28
00:02:28.373 --> 00:02:30.693
It could also contribute to repetitive firing.

29
00:02:30.693 --> 00:02:34.593
A channel calculation is not neuronal silence.

30
00:02:35.193 --> 00:02:36.793
It is certainly not a dose.
